hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24223","Hajjaj narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Farwah ibn Nawfal, from al-Harith ibn Jabalah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something to say at my sleep. He said: When you take your bed at night, recite: Say, O you disbelievers, for it is a disavowal of polytheism."
"24224","And Aswad narrated it to us, Sharik narrated to us, who said: Jabalah, and he did not doubt."
"24225","And Ali, meaning Ibn al-Madini, said: Jabalah ibn al-Harith al-Kalbi. Ali said: I heard it from Ibn Abi al-Wazir. Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: My father narrated it to us: From Ali before he was tested regarding the Qur'an."
